    <!--
        script.skinvariables replaces this default-profile fallback with the
        generated includes after Kodi has loaded the skin. Keeping it packaged
        prevents a first load or an add-on update from referencing a missing
        XML file.

        Until it does, every generated include the skin references is defined
        here as an empty stub, so that first load logs no "Skin has invalid
        include" and leaves no literal <include> inside a <content> list (which
        Kodi would fetch as the path "include"). Kodi registers an include only
        when it has a child node and inserts only its child elements, so each
        stub holds a comment: registered, inserts nothing.
    -->
